{ An identifier longer than the 255 characters this compiler keeps.

  ISO 7185 6.1.3 and ISO/IEC 10206:1991 6.1.3 make every character of an
  identifier significant, so two names that agree in their first 255 and
  differ after are *different* identifiers. This compiler keeps 255 and used
  to drop the rest in silence (StrAppend), which made them the same name: a
  program could assign to one and read the other, and a reader of the source
  would see two variables where the compiler saw one. That is worse than a
  restriction -- it is a restriction nobody is told about.

  Reported now, as the pool and the token table already report theirs. }
program identtoolong(output);
var : integer;
begin
   := 1
end.
